    {
      "id": "sce-pitch-problem-solution-market-c2",
      "heading": "Solution: five prompts",
      "explanation_md": "The **Solution** slide asks you to fill in five things:\n\n1. **Unique feature**\n2. **Significant advantage**\n3. **Major benefit**\n4. **Value proposition**\n5. **What's new about what you are doing? What are people forced to do now?**\n\nThe last prompt asks two questions together: what is new about your solution, and what people are forced to do now, without it.",
      "example_ids": [],
      "key_terms": [
        {
          "term": "Solution slide prompts",
          "meaning": "Unique feature, Significant advantage, Major benefit, Value proposition, and What's new about what you are doing? What are people forced to do now.",
          "source_ref": "sce--step-startup-pitching-template-very-early-stage#3"
        }
      ],
      "exam_line": "Solution slide: unique feature, significant advantage, major benefit, value proposition, what's new and what people are forced to do now.",
      "clarification": {
        "term": "Value proposition",
        "text": "a short statement of the value your product gives the customer and why they should choose it."
      },
